# Campaign Context Capsule Template

## Purpose

Give a cold agent the minimum campaign-level architecture and product context it could not reliably discover from the Slice alone.

## Write Here When

Create or refresh one capsule for a substantial Campaign crossing an agent, session, repository interface, or machine boundary. Reuse it across revision-compatible Slices.

## Do Not Use For

Do not use this as a task board, architecture owner, decision log, proof ledger, or substitute for canonical sources. Routine same-session work normally needs no capsule.

## Format And Profile Selection

Produce one selected profile and remove unused guidance.

- `compact`: target 500–900 tokens for a narrow Slice, context-constrained model, or project-familiar receiver when `{{OWNER_repositoryIndex}}` is current.
- `expanded`: target 1,500–3,000 tokens excluding linked source contents for a cold remote agent, shared architecture, high-risk invariants, previous regressions, or unfamiliar ownership.
- `auto`: receiver chooses, records `compact` or `expanded`, and gives one-sentence reasoning. Prefer expanded when ambiguity/risk remains; choose compact for real context constraints. Stop if mandatory context still does not fit.

An explicit sender profile wins. Compact reduces explanation, not authority or proof. Both profiles link canonical sources and retain stop conditions.

Compact normally names at most five primary and three conditional sources. Expanded normally names at most ten primary sources and does not preload conditional sources. If safe work needs more, narrow the Slice or explain the mandatory exception.

